  "section_notes": "S1 is acceptable: 24-hour serious reporting and 5-business-day other/customer notice, but other incidents are limited to confirmed ones. S2 is weakened because the 55°C test and 5% corrective-action trigger do not stop sales, favoring Northwind. S3 and S4 meet red lines with 72-month retrofit and 36-month suppression deadlines, while S5 keeps the mandatory 8/100k recall trigger and 5-business-day notices but lacks a serious-injury clause, making it acceptable."
